  "pointwise_identity": {
    "proved": true,
    "identity": "For every real symmetric zero-diagonal B and every y\u2208{\u00b11}^n:\n  \u2211_{|S|=4} \u03ba_B(S) \u220f_{v\u2208S} y_v\n    = (y\u1d40 B y)\u00b2 / 8  \u2212  (y\u1d40 B\u00b2 y) / 2  +  \u2016B\u2016_F\u00b2 / 4.",
    "proof_sketch": "Expand f=y\u1d40By=\u2211_{i\u2260j} B_ij y_i y_j. Then f\u00b2 enumerates same-edge, wedge, and disjoint edge-pair contributions. Same-edge \u2192 2\u2016B\u2016_F\u00b2 (boolean y_i\u00b2=1). Wedge \u2192 \u2016By\u2016\u00b2\u2212\u2016B\u2016_F\u00b2 after summing signed rows. Disjoint pairs: each unordered pair of vertex-disjoint edges is exactly one pairing of its 4-set, so \u2211_S \u03ba_B \u220fy equals the disj sum. Solving for that sum yields the identity. Homogeneous of degree 2 in B; constant term is \u2016B\u2016_F\u00b2/4.",
    "consequence": "E[\u2211 \u03ba_B \u220fy]=\u2211 m4 \u03ba_B = E[f\u00b2]/8 \u2212 E[\u03b3]/2 + \u2016B\u2016_F\u00b2/4 with E[\u03b3]=2\u2016B\u2016_F\u00b2 \u21d2 Q4/N=E[f\u00b2]\u22126\u2016B\u2016_F\u00b2 (typeA+wedge)."
  },
